%% Sequence — a prompt change flowing from author to production (with the eval gate).
%% Render with mermaid.live or: mmdc -i sequence-prompt-change.mmd -o sequence-prompt-change.svg
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Dev as Engineer
    participant Repo as Git (usecases/<uc>/prompts/*.prompt.yaml)
    participant PR as Pull Request
    participant CO as CODEOWNER reviewer
    participant Checks as pr-checks (lint+unit+eval subset)
    participant Full as eval-full (golden set)
    participant Deploy as deploy.yml (OIDC, environments)
    participant Reg as Runtime registry (Git cache / Langfuse / Foundry)
    participant App as Pipeline runtime

    Dev->>Repo: edit prompt YAML (bump version, changelog)
    Dev->>PR: open pull request
    PR->>CO: request review (path-owned by CODEOWNERS)
    PR->>Checks: automated checks + eval subset gate
    Checks-->>PR: pass/fail (blocks on regression)
    CO-->>PR: approve
    PR->>Repo: merge to main
    Repo->>Full: eval-full on merge (full golden set)
    Repo->>Reg: CI pushes prompt YAML to registry (if Langfuse/Foundry)
    Full-->>Deploy: pass -> trigger deploy
    Deploy->>Deploy: dev (auto)
    Deploy->>Deploy: test (needs approver + eval-full)
    Deploy->>Deploy: prod (needs approver + eval-full)
    Deploy->>App: canary 10% -> watch SLOs 15m
    alt healthy
        Deploy->>App: shift traffic to 100%
        App->>Reg: load_prompt(id, label=prod) -> new version live
    else unhealthy
        Deploy->>App: revert revision (rollback)
        Note over Reg: label 'prod' still points at previous version
    end
